# The descriptor names a flag in front of its value: the front end fills a literal at its birth up to the first member that is converted and stores the rest, so the value is stored. It lies under the name as where the allocation
# lays it, and does not go to unseen code. L0 = what is laid, L2 = the object that it is laid on.
